 20 Scenario-Based Questions on AWS Route 53
	1.	Your main application server goes down. How would you configure Route 53 to automatically redirect traffic to a backup server?
	2.	You want users from India and the US to be routed to different servers. How would you achieve this?
	3.	Your website must always route users to the server with the lowest latency. Which configuration will you use?
	4.	You need to distribute traffic between two servers in a 70:30 ratio. How do you configure this?
	5.	Your company runs an application inside a VPC and only internal users should access it. How will Route 53 help?
	6.	You want to migrate traffic slowly from an old server to a new one. How can Route 53 help in this process?
	7.	Your domain should redirect users to CloudFront for faster content delivery. How do you configure DNS records?
	8.	Users complain that sometimes your site works and sometimes it doesn’t. How would you use Route 53 health checks to troubleshoot this?
	9.	You want traffic to be routed based on user location (continent or country). How is this implemented?
	10.	You need to ensure high availability for a global application deployed in multiple AWS regions. How do you design this with Route 53?
	11.	Your website should automatically failover if the primary EC2 instance becomes unhealthy. How do you configure this?
	12.	You want to route mobile users to one endpoint and desktop users to another. How can this be achieved?
	13.	Your application is experiencing uneven traffic load. How do you balance it using Route 53?
	14.	You need to create a disaster recovery DNS strategy. What routing policies will you use?
	15.	Your domain should resolve to an Application Load Balancer. How do you configure the DNS record?
	16.	You want to test a new version of your application on a small group of users. How do you do this using Route 53?
	17.	Your DNS changes need to be propagated quickly. How can you reduce DNS caching delays?
	18.	You need to monitor endpoint availability continuously. How does Route 53 support this?
	19.	You want internal VPC services to resolve domain names without exposing them to the internet. How do you configure this?
	20.	Your multi-region architecture must ensure zero downtime even during regional failures. How do you implement DNS-based failover?
